# Account credentials for the dns01.acmeDNS solver in clusterissuer.yaml.
# Only needed if you enable apps/acme-dns -- read its README.md first.
#
# Get the values by registering once against the in-cluster acme-dns. Its API is
# ClusterIP-only, so port-forward to it:
#
#     kubectl -n acme-dns port-forward svc/acme-dns-api 8080:8080
#     curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/register | jq .
#
# Then fill this in, run ./encrypt_secrets.sh, and uncomment
# acme-dns-account.secrets.yaml in kustomization.yaml -- in the SAME commit, or
# the Kustomization can wedge (apps/acme-dns/README.md, "The two-commit
# deadlock").
#
# THE JSON KEYS ARE THE DOMAINS BEING VALIDATED, not certificate names. A
# wildcard validates at its base domain, so the *.project1-dev.devops.coop
# certificate these Gateways request needs one entry keyed
# "project1-dev.devops.coop" -- which is also the owner name of its
# _acme-challenge CNAME.
#
# One entry per validated domain, each from its OWN registration. Do not point
# several keys at one credential: acme-dns stores at most 2 TXT values per
# credential, so 3+ certificates renewing concurrently clobber each other's
# challenges.
#
# allowfrom optionally restricts which source CIDRs may update the record.
# cert-manager reaches the API over the ClusterIP, so scope it to the pod
# network if you set it at all. A wrong value here fails closed at renewal time.
#
# Keep the value valid JSON -- it is parsed, not templated, and comments cannot
# go inside the block scalar. That is also why the placeholders below are "..."
# rather than the REDACTED used in the sibling cloudflare example: detect-secrets
# flags the password key when its value looks substantive, and the usual
# allowlist pragma cannot be used inside a JSON block scalar without breaking
# the JSON.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
    name: acme-dns-account
type: Opaque
stringData:
    acmedns.json: |
        {
          "project1-dev.devops.coop": {
            "username": "...",
            "password": "...",
            "fulldomain": "....auth.project1-dev.devops.coop",
            "subdomain": "...",
            "allowfrom": []
          }
        }
